-- title:
--   Dickson's theorem for finite irreducible subgroups of GL₂
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field of characteristic $p$ with $p$ prime and $p \neq 2$, and let $H$ be a finite subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ whose order $\operatorname{card} H$ is divisible by $p$, and which is irreducible in the sense that for every non-zero vector $v \in K^2$ there is some $h \in H$ with $h \cdot v \notin K v$ (the matrix acting on $v$ by `*ᵥ`, the line being the $K$-span of $v$). Then at least one of the following holds: either $p = 3$ and $9 \nmid \operatorname{card} H$; or there exist a subfield $F \subseteq K$ which is finite, together with $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$, such that (i) for every $s \in \mathrm{SL}_2(F)$ the element $g \, s \, g^{-1}$, formed after pushing $s$ forward along the inclusion $F \hookrightarrow K$ and viewing it in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$, lies in $H$, and (ii) every $h \in H$ satisfies $g^{-1} h g = a \cdot m$ as a matrix over $K$, for some scalar $a \in K$ and some $m \in \mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ mapped into $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ along the same inclusion. Thus in the second case $g\,\mathrm{SL}_2(F)\,g^{-1} \subseteq H \subseteq g\,(K^\times \cdot \mathrm{GL}_2(F))\,g^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the part of Dickson's classification of the finite subgroups of $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over a field of characteristic $p$ that concerns subgroups of order divisible by $p$: such a subgroup either fixes a line, or has projective image conjugate to $\mathrm{PSL}_2(\mathbb{F}_q)$ or $\mathrm{PGL}_2(\mathbb{F}_q)$ for a power $q$ of $p$, or $p = 3$ and the exceptional case occurs, detected here by $9 \nmid \operatorname{card} H$. The proof cites [`Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.exists_subfield_forall_upperElem_mem_iff_of_finite`](thm.html#Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.exists_subfield_forall_upperElem_mem_iff_of_finite), which identifies the field generated by the unipotent elements of a finite subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(K)$ containing a non-trivial upper and a non-trivial lower elementary matrix; the result is used in the vanishing of the first cohomology of the trace-zero adjoint twist for representations with finite image.
-- source:
